      "sourcePath": "content/materials/4-rare/metals/bismuth-ingot/index.md",
      "sourceFolder": "content/materials/4-rare/metals/bismuth-ingot",
      "content": "---\ntitle: Bismuth Ingot\nslug: bismuth-ingot\ntype: item\nkingdom: Material\nitem_class: Rare\ncategory: Ingot\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ingot\nmaterial_family: Bismuth\nsource_items:\n  - Bismuth Ore\nweight: 0.8kg\nweight_class: Light\ndurability: Low\nenchantment_affinity: \"75% (+6 dice)\"\ndamage_modifier: 4\narmor_modifier: 1\nmarket_value: 75 Marks\ntags:\n  - items\n  - materials\n  - metal\n  - ingot\n  - rare\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Bismuth Ingot\n\n## Effect\nBismuth Ingots produce a highly unstable metal that dramatically increases power output while introducing unpredictability into both physical and magical performance.\n\n---\n## Appearance\nBismuth Ingots retain their distinctive crystalline geometry, forming angular, stepped patterns rather than smooth bars. Their surface shimmers with metallic rainbow hues that seem to move across the metal like a slow pulse.\n\nWhen exposed to magical energy or stress, faint distortions ripple across the ingot’s surface, giving the impression that the metal is constantly on the verge of shifting or fracturing.\n\n---\n## Crafting Use\n- Experimental weapons  \n- Arcane constructs  \n- Chaos-based gear  \n- High-risk enchantment platforms  \n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Brittle and structurally inconsistent  \n- Highly reactive to magical input  \n- Can shift or fracture under extreme conditions  \n- Unreliable under sustained pressure  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Extremely high affinity with chaotic or volatile magic  \n- Enhances:\n  - Burst damage  \n  - Wild magic effects  \n  - High-risk enchantments  \n- Increased chance of instability or backlash  \n\n---\n\n## Combat Integration\n- +4 Damage Modifier  \n- +1 Armor Modifier  \n- High-risk, high-reward material  \n\n---\n\n## Crafting Source\n- Requires: 4x [[Bismuth Ore]]\n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"Power without control is still power — just not yours.\"*\n",
      "body": "# Bismuth Ingot\n\n## Effect\nBismuth Ingots produce a highly unstable metal that dramatically increases power output while introducing unpredictability into both physical and magical performance.\n\n---\n## Appearance\nBismuth Ingots retain their distinctive crystalline geometry, forming angular, stepped patterns rather than smooth bars. Their surface shimmers with metallic rainbow hues that seem to move across the metal like a slow pulse.\n\nWhen exposed to magical energy or stress, faint distortions ripple across the ingot’s surface, giving the impression that the metal is constantly on the verge of shifting or fracturing.\n\n---\n## Crafting Use\n- Experimental weapons  \n- Arcane constructs  \n- Chaos-based gear  \n- High-risk enchantment platforms  \n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Brittle and structurally inconsistent  \n- Highly reactive to magical input  \n- Can shift or fracture under extreme conditions  \n- Unreliable under sustained pressure  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Extremely high affinity with chaotic or volatile magic  \n- Enhances:\n  - Burst damage  \n  - Wild magic effects  \n  - High-risk enchantments  \n- Increased chance of instability or backlash  \n\n---\n\n## Combat Integration\n- +4 Damage Modifier  \n- +1 Armor Modifier  \n- High-risk, high-reward material  \n\n---\n\n## Crafting Source\n- Requires: 4x [[Bismuth Ore]]\n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"Power without control is still power — just not yours.\"*",
