      "content": "---\ntitle: Glass Ingot\nslug: glass-ingot\ntype: item\nkingdom: Material\nitem_class: Rare\ncategory: Ingot\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ingot (Alloy)\nmaterial_family: Glass\nsource_items:\n  - Astryx Sand\n  - Aluminum Ingot\nweight: 0.6kg\nweight_class: Very Light\ndurability: Moderate\nenchantment_affinity: \"70% (+5 dice)\"\ndamage_modifier: +4\narmor_modifier: +1\nmarket_value: 160–260 Marks (Rare Trade)\ntags:\n  - items\n  - materials\n  - metal\n  - ingot\n  - rare\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Glass Ingot\n\n## Effect\nGlass is a specialised crystalline alloy formed by fusing Astryx Sand with Aluminum through a controlled magical forging process. The result is a hardened material that combines clarity, sharpness, and precision.\n\nIt excels in focused output and cutting power but is vulnerable to heavy impacts.\n\n---\n## Appearance\nGlass Ingots are smooth, semi-transparent bars with a polished surface that refracts light into shifting prismatic patterns. Internal layers appear suspended within the material, giving it depth and clarity.\n\nEdges form with unnatural sharpness, and the surface reflects light in clean, precise lines.\n\n---\n## Lore\nGlass is created from **Astryx Sand**, a rare silica found in magically active regions, combined with Aluminum to stabilise its structure during forging. Through careful refinement, this fragile material is transformed into a hardened alloy capable of rivaling rare metals in performance.\n\nEarly attempts to create Glass often resulted in catastrophic fractures, and even now, only skilled artisans can produce it reliably.\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Extremely sharp and precise  \n- Lightweight and easy to handle  \n- Structurally strong but brittle under impact  \n- Requires precise crafting techniques  \n\n---\n\n## Alloy Composition\n- Astryx Sand  \n- Aluminum Ingot  \n- Controlled magical forging process  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- High affinity with **Light** and **Air**  \n- Enhances:\n  - Precision-based effects  \n  - Light manipulation  \n  - Illusion-based enchantments  \n- Poor performance under heavy or destructive enchantments  \n\n---\n\n## Combat Integration\n- +4 Damage Modifier  \n- +1 Armor Modifier  \n- Favours precision, burst damage, and high-skill builds  \n\n---\n\n## Crafting Source\n- Requires Astryx Sand  \n- Requires Aluminum Ingot  \n- Requires specialised stabilisation forge  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It is not fragile — it simply refuses to bend.\"*\n",
      "body": "# Glass Ingot\n\n## Effect\nGlass is a specialised crystalline alloy formed by fusing Astryx Sand with Aluminum through a controlled magical forging process. The result is a hardened material that combines clarity, sharpness, and precision.\n\nIt excels in focused output and cutting power but is vulnerable to heavy impacts.\n\n---\n## Appearance\nGlass Ingots are smooth, semi-transparent bars with a polished surface that refracts light into shifting prismatic patterns. Internal layers appear suspended within the material, giving it depth and clarity.\n\nEdges form with unnatural sharpness, and the surface reflects light in clean, precise lines.\n\n---\n## Lore\nGlass is created from **Astryx Sand**, a rare silica found in magically active regions, combined with Aluminum to stabilise its structure during forging. Through careful refinement, this fragile material is transformed into a hardened alloy capable of rivaling rare metals in performance.\n\nEarly attempts to create Glass often resulted in catastrophic fractures, and even now, only skilled artisans can produce it reliably.\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Extremely sharp and precise  \n- Lightweight and easy to handle  \n- Structurally strong but brittle under impact  \n- Requires precise crafting techniques  \n\n---\n\n## Alloy Composition\n- Astryx Sand  \n- Aluminum Ingot  \n- Controlled magical forging process  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- High affinity with **Light** and **Air**  \n- Enhances:\n  - Precision-based effects  \n  - Light manipulation  \n  - Illusion-based enchantments  \n- Poor performance under heavy or destructive enchantments  \n\n---\n\n## Combat Integration\n- +4 Damage Modifier  \n- +1 Armor Modifier  \n- Favours precision, burst damage, and high-skill builds  \n\n---\n\n## Crafting Source\n- Requires Astryx Sand  \n- Requires Aluminum Ingot  \n- Requires specialised stabilisation forge  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It is not fragile — it simply refuses to bend.\"*",
