      "content": "---\ntitle: Tin Ingot\nslug: tin-ingot\ntype: item\nkingdom: Material\nitem_class: Common\ncategory: Ingot\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ingot\nmaterial_family: Tin\nsource_items:\n  - Tin Ore\nweight: 0.9kg\nweight_class: Light\ndurability: Low\nenchantment_affinity: \"10% (+0 dice)\"\nmarket_value: 4 Marks\ntags:\n  - items\n  - materials\n  - metal\n  - ingot\n  - common\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Tin Ingot\n\n## Effect\nA refined but weak metal, Tin Ingots are primarily used as a stabilising component in alloy crafting rather than for direct equipment creation.\n\n---\n\n## Crafting Use\n- Core component for Bronze\n- Used in beginner alloy recipes\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Very soft and flexible  \n- Cannot hold an edge  \n- Supports alloy integrity  \n\n---\n\n## Alloy Use\n- [[Bronze Ingot]]\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Enhances enchantment stability in alloys  \n- Reduces magical backlash  \n\n---\n\n## Crafting Source\n- Requires: 4x [[Tin Ore]]\n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"Strength is not always found in the metal itself, but in what it allows.\"*\n",
