      "route": "/compendium/item/resources-and-materials/metal/metal-ingots/titan-steel-ingot",
      "sourcePath": "content/materials/5-epic/metals/titan-steel-ingot/index.md",
      "sourceFolder": "content/materials/5-epic/metals/titan-steel-ingot",
      "content": "---\ntitle: Titan Steel Ingot\nslug: titan-steel-ingot\ntype: item\nkingdom: Material\nitem_class: Epic\ncategory: Ingot\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ingot (Alloy)\nmaterial_family: Titan Steel\nsource_items:\n  - High Steel\n  - Titan Blood\nweight: 2.5kg\nweight_class: Heavy\ndurability: Extreme\nenchantment_affinity: \"65% (+5 dice)\"\ndamage_modifier: +5\narmor_modifier: +5\nmarket_value: 300–500 Marks (Mythic Trade)\ntags:\n  - items\n  - materials\n  - metal\n  - ingot\n  - epic\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Titan Steel Ingot\n\n## Effect\nTitan Steel is a legendary alloy forged by infusing High Steel with the blood of the Titan race. It embodies unmatched physical strength and resilience, allowing it to endure and deliver immense force without compromise.\n\n---\n\n## Appearance\nTitan Steel appears as a dense, dark metallic alloy with faint, slow-moving veins of deep amber or gold running beneath its surface. These veins pulse subtly, as if carrying the lingering essence of something immense and ancient.\n\nThe metal feels impossibly heavy for its size, and even at rest, it gives the impression of contained force.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nTitan Steel is not merely forged — it is created through sacrifice.\n\nThe process requires High Steel to be infused with the essence of a Titan, a race of lesser gods whose existence is rare and dwindling. Because of this, Titan Steel is one of the most difficult materials to create, and its existence is tightly controlled across the realms.\n\nMany believe that each ingot retains a fragment of the Titan’s will, granting it strength beyond mortal materials.\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Extremely dense and heavy  \n- Unmatched resistance to physical force  \n- Maintains integrity under extreme stress  \n- Difficult to shape and nearly impossible to break  \n\n---\n\n## Alloy Composition\n- High Steel  \n- Titan Blood (or preserved Titan essence)  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Moderate affinity with **Earth**  \n- Enhances:\n  - Strength-based effects  \n  - Impact and force  \n  - Defensive enchantments  \n- Poor synergy with delicate or precision-based enchantments  \n\n---\n\n## Combat Integration\n- +5 Damage Modifier  \n- +5 Armor Modifier  \n- Favours heavy, strength-based, and frontline builds  \n\n---\n\n## Special Interaction\n- Increased effectiveness against massive or high-tier creatures  \n- Cannot be easily broken, sundered, or degraded  \n- Performs best under direct physical confrontation  \n\n---\n\n## Crafting Source\n- Requires High Steel  \n- Requires Titan Blood or Titan essence  \n- Requires advanced or divine-grade forge  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It does not yield — it reminds the world what strength truly is.\"*\n",
      "body": "# Titan Steel Ingot\n\n## Effect\nTitan Steel is a legendary alloy forged by infusing High Steel with the blood of the Titan race. It embodies unmatched physical strength and resilience, allowing it to endure and deliver immense force without compromise.\n\n---\n\n## Appearance\nTitan Steel appears as a dense, dark metallic alloy with faint, slow-moving veins of deep amber or gold running beneath its surface. These veins pulse subtly, as if carrying the lingering essence of something immense and ancient.\n\nThe metal feels impossibly heavy for its size, and even at rest, it gives the impression of contained force.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nTitan Steel is not merely forged — it is created through sacrifice.\n\nThe process requires High Steel to be infused with the essence of a Titan, a race of lesser gods whose existence is rare and dwindling. Because of this, Titan Steel is one of the most difficult materials to create, and its existence is tightly controlled across the realms.\n\nMany believe that each ingot retains a fragment of the Titan’s will, granting it strength beyond mortal materials.\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Extremely dense and heavy  \n- Unmatched resistance to physical force  \n- Maintains integrity under extreme stress  \n- Difficult to shape and nearly impossible to break  \n\n---\n\n## Alloy Composition\n- High Steel  \n- Titan Blood (or preserved Titan essence)  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Moderate affinity with **Earth**  \n- Enhances:\n  - Strength-based effects  \n  - Impact and force  \n  - Defensive enchantments  \n- Poor synergy with delicate or precision-based enchantments  \n\n---\n\n## Combat Integration\n- +5 Damage Modifier  \n- +5 Armor Modifier  \n- Favours heavy, strength-based, and frontline builds  \n\n---\n\n## Special Interaction\n- Increased effectiveness against massive or high-tier creatures  \n- Cannot be easily broken, sundered, or degraded  \n- Performs best under direct physical confrontation  \n\n---\n\n## Crafting Source\n- Requires High Steel  \n- Requires Titan Blood or Titan essence  \n- Requires advanced or divine-grade forge  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It does not yield — it reminds the world what strength truly is.\"*",
