      "sourcePath": "content/minerals/1-common/ores/antimony-ore/index.md",
      "sourceFolder": "content/minerals/1-common/ores/antimony-ore",
      "content": "---\ntitle: Antimony Ore\nslug: antimony-ore\ntype: item\nkingdom: Mineral\nitem_class: Common\ncategory: Ore\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ore\nmaterial_family: Antimony\nsource_items: []\nrefines_into: Antimony Ingot\nrefinement_ratio: \"4:1\"\nweight_class: Light\ndurability: Low\nenchantment_affinity: \"12% (+0 dice)\"\nmarket_value: 3 Marks\nimage: Antimony Ore.png\ntags:\n  - items\n  - minerals\n  - metal\n  - ore\n  - common\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Antimony Ore\n\n## Effect\nAntimony Ore is a brittle, crystalline metal-bearing ore that enhances hardness and structural integrity when alloyed. It is rarely used alone but is critical in reinforcing softer metals.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nKnown as the *“Bone of the Earth,”* antimony was believed by ancient smiths to give metals their “spine.” While fragile in isolation, it grants resilience to those it strengthens.\n\n---\n\n## Material & Crafting Traits\n- Brittle and unstable in raw form  \n- Breaks easily under stress  \n- Essential for strengthening alloys  \n- Requires careful refinement  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Antimony Ingot]]\n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot\n- Notes: Fragile structure leads to material loss if overheated\n\n---\n\n## Alloy Use\n- [[Pewter Ingot]]\n- Future reinforced alloys\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Slightly improves structural stability of enchanted items  \n- Helps prevent deformation under magical stress  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It does not endure — it ensures that others do.\"*\n",
      "body": "# Antimony Ore\n\n## Effect\nAntimony Ore is a brittle, crystalline metal-bearing ore that enhances hardness and structural integrity when alloyed. It is rarely used alone but is critical in reinforcing softer metals.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nKnown as the *“Bone of the Earth,”* antimony was believed by ancient smiths to give metals their “spine.” While fragile in isolation, it grants resilience to those it strengthens.\n\n---\n\n## Material & Crafting Traits\n- Brittle and unstable in raw form  \n- Breaks easily under stress  \n- Essential for strengthening alloys  \n- Requires careful refinement  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Antimony Ingot]]\n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot\n- Notes: Fragile structure leads to material loss if overheated\n\n---\n\n## Alloy Use\n- [[Pewter Ingot]]\n- Future reinforced alloys\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Slightly improves structural stability of enchanted items  \n- Helps prevent deformation under magical stress  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It does not endure — it ensures that others do.\"*",
      "sections": {
        "Overview": "# Antimony Ore",
        "Effect": "Antimony Ore is a brittle, crystalline metal-bearing ore that enhances hardness and structural integrity when alloyed. It is rarely used alone but is critical in reinforcing softer metals.\n\n---",
        "Lore": "Known as the *“Bone of the Earth,”* antimony was believed by ancient smiths to give metals their “spine.” While fragile in isolation, it grants resilience to those it strengthens.\n\n---",
        "Material & Crafting Traits": "- Brittle and unstable in raw form  \n- Breaks easily under stress  \n- Essential for strengthening alloys  \n- Requires careful refinement  \n\n---",
        "Refinement": "- Smelts into: [[Antimony Ingot]]\n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot\n- Notes: Fragile structure leads to material loss if overheated\n\n---",
        "Alloy Use": "- [[Pewter Ingot]]\n- Future reinforced alloys\n\n---",
        "Enchantment Use": "- Slightly improves structural stability of enchanted items  \n- Helps prevent deformation under magical stress  \n\n---",
        "Quote": "*\"It does not endure — it ensures that others do.\"*"
      },
