      "searchTerms": "dark silver ore item resources & materials metal metal ores {\"title\":\"dark silver ore\",\"slug\":\"dark-silver-ore\",\"type\":\"item\",\"kingdom\":\"mineral\",\"itemclass\":\"rare\",\"category\":\"ore\",\"subcategory\":\"metal\",\"materialtype\":\"metal\",\"materialform\":\"ore\",\"materialfamily\":\"dark silver\",\"sourceitems\":[],\"refinesinto\":\"dark silver ingot\",\"refinementratio\":\"4:1\",\"weightclass\":\"light\",\"durability\":\"high\",\"enchantmentaffinity\":\"60% (+4 dice)\",\"marketvalue\":\"20 marks\",\"tags\":[\"items\",\"minerals\",\"metal\",\"ore\",\"rare\"],\"visibility\":\"public\"} # dark silver ore\n\n## effect\ndark silver ore is infused with the primordial essence of **dark itself** — not death, but absence, depth, and shadow. it absorbs light and distorts magical energy, forming a metal that thrives in low-light environments.\n\n---\n## appearance\ndark silver ore appears as smooth, shadow-toned metal veined through stone, with a muted, almost matte finish that absorbs surrounding light. its surface reflects very little, giving it a depth that feels more like a void than a solid material.\n\nin low light, faint ripples of darker shade seem to move across the ore, as though shadows are pooling and shifting within it rather than around it.\n\n---\n## lore\ndark silver was not mined — it was *formed*. in places where light was stripped away completely, the essence of dark condensed into physical form. it is neither evil nor corrupt, but a reflection of balance — the quiet counterpart to light.\n\n---\n\n## material & crafting traits\n- absorbs ambient light and magical energy  \n- strengthens in darkness and shadow-rich environments  \n- naturally dampens radiant and light-based effects  \n- stable during refinement despite its unusual origin  \n\n---\n\n## refinement\n- smelts into: [[dark silver ingot]]  \n- ratio: 4 ore → 1 ingot  \n- notes: best refined in low-light or magically controlled environments  \n\n---\n\n## alloy use\n- dark-aligned alloys (future)\n\n---\n\n## enchantment use\n- high affinity with **dark** magic  \n- supports shadow manipulation and concealment effects  \n- reduces stability of light-based enchantments  \n\n---\n\n## quote\n*\"it is not the absence of light — it is what remains when light leaves.\"*"
