      "content": "---\ntitle: Ebony Ore\nslug: ebony-ore\ntype: item\nkingdom: Mineral\nitem_class: Epic\ncategory: Ore\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ore\nmaterial_family: Ebony\nsource_items: []\nrefines_into: Ebony Ingot\nrefinement_ratio: \"4:1\"\nweight_class: Medium\ndurability: High\nenchantment_affinity: \"65% (+5 dice)\"\nmarket_value: 220–350 Marks (Restricted Trade)\ntags:\n  - items\n  - minerals\n  - metal\n  - ore\n  - epic\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Ebony Ore\n\n## Effect\nEbony Ore is a naturally occurring shadow-infused metal that absorbs light and ambient energy. It suppresses presence and reduces magical visibility, making it ideal for stealth and concealment.\n\n---\n\n## Appearance\nEbony Ore appears as deep black stone with a matte surface that absorbs surrounding light. Faint violet undertones can be seen within its structure when exposed to magical energy.\n\nIts edges seem to blur slightly in low light, as though the material is partially merging with shadow.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nEbony forms deep within the Netherworld and other shadow-aligned regions, where light cannot reach and death energy accumulates over time.\n\nIt is often associated with ancient entities and forgotten places, and those who mine it report an unnatural silence surrounding the material.\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Absorbs light and ambient energy  \n- Dampens sound and presence  \n- Stable under shadow and death energy  \n- Difficult to detect in low-light environments  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Ebony Ingot]]  \n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot  \n- Requires shadow-aligned forge or controlled environment  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Strong affinity with **Dark** and **Death**  \n- Enhances:\n  - Stealth effects  \n  - Energy drain  \n  - Suppression abilities  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"Where light ends, it begins.\"*\n",
      "body": "# Ebony Ore\n\n## Effect\nEbony Ore is a naturally occurring shadow-infused metal that absorbs light and ambient energy. It suppresses presence and reduces magical visibility, making it ideal for stealth and concealment.\n\n---\n\n## Appearance\nEbony Ore appears as deep black stone with a matte surface that absorbs surrounding light. Faint violet undertones can be seen within its structure when exposed to magical energy.\n\nIts edges seem to blur slightly in low light, as though the material is partially merging with shadow.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nEbony forms deep within the Netherworld and other shadow-aligned regions, where light cannot reach and death energy accumulates over time.\n\nIt is often associated with ancient entities and forgotten places, and those who mine it report an unnatural silence surrounding the material.\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Absorbs light and ambient energy  \n- Dampens sound and presence  \n- Stable under shadow and death energy  \n- Difficult to detect in low-light environments  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Ebony Ingot]]  \n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot  \n- Requires shadow-aligned forge or controlled environment  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Strong affinity with **Dark** and **Death**  \n- Enhances:\n  - Stealth effects  \n  - Energy drain  \n  - Suppression abilities  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"Where light ends, it begins.\"*",
