      "content": "---\ntitle: Elementium Ore\nslug: elementium-ore\ntype: item\nkingdom: Mineral\nitem_class: Mythic\ncategory: Ore\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ore\nmaterial_family: Elementium\nsource_items: []\nrefines_into: Elementium Ingot\nrefinement_ratio: \"4:1\"\nformation_type: Leyline / Elemental Convergence\nweight_class: Medium\ndurability: Very High\nelemental_alignment:\n  - Fire\n  - Water\n  - Earth\n  - Air\n  - Light\n  - Dark\n  - Life\n  - Death\nenchantment_affinity: \"85% (+7 dice)\"\nmarket_value: 500–800 Marks (Mythic Trade)\ntags:\n  - items\n  - minerals\n  - metal\n  - ore\n  - mythic\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Elementium Ore\n\n## Effect\nElementium Ore is a rare elemental metal formed where powerful ley lines and elemental forces converge. The ore naturally harmonises surrounding energies, allowing it to stabilise and conduct multiple elemental alignments simultaneously.\n\n---\n\n## Appearance\nElementium Ore appears as dark metallic stone threaded with shifting veins of elemental colour. These veins pulse softly and change depending on the surrounding elemental environment.\n\nNear fire the ore glows amber-red, while near water it shifts toward deep blue and silver tones.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nElementium Ore forms in regions where elemental energy reaches perfect balance — ancient leyline nexuses, elemental convergence zones, or shattered locations touched by multiple realms.\n\nMany scholars believe the material is not forged by the elements, but created by their agreement to coexist.\n\nFragments of Elementium can alter the surrounding ecosystem over time, slowly reshaping environments to reflect elemental balance.\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Harmonises multiple elemental energies  \n- Stable under magical stress  \n- Conducts elemental mana efficiently  \n- Slowly adapts to surrounding elemental environments  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Elementium Ingot]]  \n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot  \n- Requires elemental convergence forge or astral forge conditions  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Exceptional affinity with elemental enchantments  \n- Enhances:\n  - Elemental harmony  \n  - Mana stability  \n  - Multi-element enchantments  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"The elements do not fight within it — they listen.\"*\n",
      "body": "# Elementium Ore\n\n## Effect\nElementium Ore is a rare elemental metal formed where powerful ley lines and elemental forces converge. The ore naturally harmonises surrounding energies, allowing it to stabilise and conduct multiple elemental alignments simultaneously.\n\n---\n\n## Appearance\nElementium Ore appears as dark metallic stone threaded with shifting veins of elemental colour. These veins pulse softly and change depending on the surrounding elemental environment.\n\nNear fire the ore glows amber-red, while near water it shifts toward deep blue and silver tones.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nElementium Ore forms in regions where elemental energy reaches perfect balance — ancient leyline nexuses, elemental convergence zones, or shattered locations touched by multiple realms.\n\nMany scholars believe the material is not forged by the elements, but created by their agreement to coexist.\n\nFragments of Elementium can alter the surrounding ecosystem over time, slowly reshaping environments to reflect elemental balance.\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Harmonises multiple elemental energies  \n- Stable under magical stress  \n- Conducts elemental mana efficiently  \n- Slowly adapts to surrounding elemental environments  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Elementium Ingot]]  \n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot  \n- Requires elemental convergence forge or astral forge conditions  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Exceptional affinity with elemental enchantments  \n- Enhances:\n  - Elemental harmony  \n  - Mana stability  \n  - Multi-element enchantments  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"The elements do not fight within it — they listen.\"*",
