      "content": "---\ntitle: Zinc Ore\nslug: zinc-ore\ntype: item\nkingdom: Mineral\nitem_class: Common\ncategory: Ore\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ore\nmaterial_family: Zinc\nsource_items: []\nrefines_into: Zinc Ingot\nrefinement_ratio: \"4:1\"\nweight_class: Light\ndurability: Low\nenchantment_affinity: \"10% (+0 dice)\"\nmarket_value: 2 Marks\ntags:\n  - items\n  - minerals\n  - metal\n  - ore\n  - common\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Zinc Ore\n\n## Effect\nZinc Ore is a reactive and volatile material that plays a critical role in alloy creation. While weak on its own, it enhances flexibility, resonance, and thermal response when combined with other metals.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nKnown as the *“Breath of the Forge,”* zinc was discovered not for its strength, but for how it transformed other metals. Ancient artificers prized it for its ability to “awaken” dormant properties within alloys.\n\n---\n\n## Material & Crafting Traits\n- Low structural strength  \n- Highly reactive when heated  \n- Vaporises at high temperatures if mishandled  \n- Essential for alloy crafting  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Zinc Ingot]]\n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot\n- Notes: Requires controlled heat to prevent material loss\n\n---\n\n## Alloy Use\n- [[Brass Ingot]]\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Minimal direct use  \n- Enhances resonance in alloys  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It is not the strength of zinc, but what it awakens in others.\"*\n",
      "body": "# Zinc Ore\n\n## Effect\nZinc Ore is a reactive and volatile material that plays a critical role in alloy creation. While weak on its own, it enhances flexibility, resonance, and thermal response when combined with other metals.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nKnown as the *“Breath of the Forge,”* zinc was discovered not for its strength, but for how it transformed other metals. Ancient artificers prized it for its ability to “awaken” dormant properties within alloys.\n\n---\n\n## Material & Crafting Traits\n- Low structural strength  \n- Highly reactive when heated  \n- Vaporises at high temperatures if mishandled  \n- Essential for alloy crafting  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Zinc Ingot]]\n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot\n- Notes: Requires controlled heat to prevent material loss\n\n---\n\n## Alloy Use\n- [[Brass Ingot]]\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Minimal direct use  \n- Enhances resonance in alloys  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It is not the strength of zinc, but what it awakens in others.\"*",
